.TH ORO-OS-CONSTANTS 3 "" "Oro Runtime" "Oro Runtime API Manual"
.SH NAME
oro:os/constants \- JavaScript API module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
import * as module from 'oro:os/constants'
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
oro:os/constants is a JavaScript API module exposed by the Oro Runtime.
.SH REFERENCE
.TP
\fBerrno\fR
A container for all known "errno" constant values. Unsupported values have a default value of `0`.
.TP
\fBE2BIG()\fR
"Arg list too long" The number of bytes used for the argument and environment list of the new process exceeded the limit NCARGS (specified in ⟨sys/param.h⟩).
.TP
\fBEACCES()\fR
"Permission denied" An attempt was made to access a file in a way forbidden by its file access permissions.
.TP
\fBEADDRINUSE()\fR
"Address already in use" Only one usage of each address is normally permitted.
.TP
\fBEADDRNOTAVAIL()\fR
"Cannot assign requested address" Normally results from an attempt to create a socket with an address not on this machine.
.TP
\fBEAFNOSUPPORT()\fR
"Address family not supported by protocol family" An address incompatible with the requested protocol was used. For example, you shouldn't necessarily expect to be able to use NS addresses with ARPA Internet protocols.
.TP
\fBEAGAIN()\fR
"Resource temporarily unavailable" This is a temporary condition and later calls to the same routine may complete normally.
.TP
\fBEALREADY()\fR
"Operation already in progress" An operation was attempted on a non\-blocking object that already had an operation in progress.
.TP
\fBEBADF()\fR
"Bad file descriptor" A file descriptor argument was out of range, referred to no open file, or a read (write) request was made to a file that was only open for writing (reading).
.TP
\fBEBADMSG()\fR
"Bad message" The message to be received is inapprorpiate for the operation being attempted.
.TP
\fBEBUSY()\fR
"Resource busy" An attempt to use a system resource which was in use at the time in a manner which would have conflicted with the request.
.TP
\fBECANCELED()\fR
"Operation canceled" The scheduled operation was canceled.
.TP
\fBECHILD()\fR
"No child processes" A wait or waitpid function was executed by a process that had no existing or unwaited\-for child processes.
.TP
\fBECONNABORTED()\fR
"Software caused connection abort" A connection abort was caused internal to your host machine.
.TP
\fBECONNREFUSED()\fR
"Connection refused" No connection could be made because the target machine actively refused it. This usually results from trying to connect to a service that is inactive on the foreign host.
.TP
\fBECONNRESET()\fR
"Connection reset by peer" A connection was forcibly closed by a peer. This normally results from a loss of the connection on the remote socket due to a timeout or a reboot.
.TP
\fBEDEADLK()\fR
"Resource deadlock avoided" An attempt was made to lock a system resource that would have resulted in a deadlock situation.
.TP
\fBEDESTADDRREQ()\fR
"Destination address required" A required address was omitted from an operation on a socket.
.TP
\fBEDOM()\fR
"Numerical argument out of domain" A numerical input argument was outside the defined domain of the mathematical function.
.TP
\fBEDQUOT()\fR
"Disc quota exceeded" A write to an ordinary file, the creation of a directory or symbolic link, or the creation of a directory entry failed because the user's quota of disk blocks was exhausted, or the allocation of an inode for a newly created file failed because the user's quota of inodes was exhausted.
.TP
\fBEEXIST()\fR
"File exists" An existing file was mentioned in an inappropriate context, for instance, as the new link name in a link function.
.TP
\fBEFAULT()\fR
"Bad address" The system detected an invalid address in attempting to use an argument of a call.
.TP
\fBEFBIG()\fR
"File too large" The size of a file exceeded the maximum.
.TP
\fBEHOSTUNREACH()\fR
"No route to host" A socket operation was attempted to an unreachable host.
.TP
\fBEIDRM()\fR
"Identifier removed" An IPC identifier was removed while the current process was waiting on it.
.TP
\fBEILSEQ()\fR
"Illegal byte sequence" While decoding a multibyte character the function came along an invalid or an incomplete sequence of bytes or the given wide character is invalid.
.TP
\fBEINPROGRESS()\fR
"Operation now in progress" An operation that takes a long time to complete.
.TP
\fBEINTR()\fR
"Interrupted function call" An asynchronous signal (such as SIGINT or SIGQUIT) was caught by the process during the execution of an interruptible function. If the signal handler performs a normal return, the interrupted function call will seem to have returned the error condition.
.TP
\fBEINVAL()\fR
"Invalid argument" Some invalid argument was supplied. (For example, specifying an undefined signal to a signal or kill function).
.TP
\fBEIO()\fR
"Input/output error" Some physical input or output error occurred. This error will not be reported until a subsequent operation on the same file descriptor and may be lost (over written) by any subsequent errors.
.TP
\fBEISCONN()\fR
"Socket is already connected" A connect or connectx request was made on an already connected socket; or, a sendto or sendmsg request on a connected socket specified a destination when already connected.
.TP
\fBEISDIR()\fR
"Is a directory" An attempt was made to open a directory with write mode specified.
.TP
\fBELOOP()\fR
"Too many levels of symbolic links" A path name lookup involved more than 8 symbolic links.
.TP
\fBEMFILE()\fR
"Too many open files"
.TP
\fBEMLINK()\fR
"Too many links" Maximum allowable hard links to a single file has been exceeded (limit of 32767 hard links per file).
.TP
\fBEMSGSIZE()\fR
"Message too long" A message sent on a socket was larger than the internal message buffer or some other network limit.
.TP
\fBEMULTIHOP()\fR
"Reserved" This error is reserved for future use.
.TP
\fBENAMETOOLONG()\fR
"File name too long" A component of a path name exceeded 255 (MAXNAMELEN) characters, or an entire path name exceeded 1023 (MAXPATHLEN\-1) characters.
.TP
\fBENETDOWN()\fR
"Network is down" A socket operation encountered a dead network.
.TP
\fBENETRESET()\fR
"Network dropped connection on reset" The host you were connected to crashed and rebooted.
.TP
\fBENETUNREACH()\fR
"Network is unreachable" A socket operation was attempted to an unreachable network.
.TP
\fBENFILE()\fR
"Too many open files in system" Maximum number of file descriptors allowable on the system has been reached and a requests for an open cannot be satisfied until at least one has been closed.
.TP
\fBENOBUFS()\fR
"No buffer space available" An operation on a socket or pipe was not performed because the system lacked sufficient buffer space or because a queue was full.
.TP
\fBENODATA()\fR
"No message available" No message was available to be received by the requested operation.
.TP
\fBENODEV()\fR
"Operation not supported by device" An attempt was made to apply an inappropriate function to a device, for example, trying to read a write\-only device such as a printer.
.TP
\fBENOENT()\fR
"No such file or directory" A component of a specified pathname did not exist, or the pathname was an empty string.
.TP
\fBENOEXEC()\fR
"Exec format error" A request was made to execute a file that, although it has the appropriate permissions, was not in the format required for an executable file.
.TP
\fBENOLCK()\fR
"No locks available" A system\-imposed limit on the number of simultaneous file locks was reached.
.TP
\fBENOLINK()\fR
"Reserved" This error is reserved for future use.
.TP
\fBENOMEM()\fR
"Cannot allocate memory" The new process image required more memory than was allowed by the hardware or by system\-imposed memory management constraints.A lack of swap space is normally temporary; however, a lack of core is not. Soft limits may be increased to their corresponding hard limits.
.TP
\fBENOMSG()\fR
"No message of desired type" An IPC message queue does not contain a message of the desired type, or a message catalog does not contain the requested message.
.TP
\fBENOPROTOOPT()\fR
"Protocol not available" A bad option or level was specified in a `getsockopt(2)` or `setsockopt(2)` call.
.TP
\fBENOSPC()\fR
"Device out of space" A write to an ordinary file, the creation of a directory or symbolic link, or the creation of a directory entry failed because no more disk blocks were available on the file system, or the allocation of an inode for a newly created file failed because no more inodes were available on the file system.
.TP
\fBENOSR()\fR
"No STREAM resources" This error is reserved for future use.
.TP
\fBENOSTR()\fR
"Not a STREAM" This error is reserved for future use.
.TP
\fBENOSYS()\fR
"Function not implemented" Attempted a system call that is not available on this system.
.TP
\fBENOTCONN()\fR
"Socket is not connected" An request to send or receive data was disallowed because the socket was not connected and (when sending on a datagram socket) no address was supplied.
.TP
\fBENOTDIR()\fR
"Not a directory" A component of the specified pathname existed, but it was not a directory, when a directory was expected.
.TP
\fBENOTEMPTY()\fR
"Directory not empty" A directory with entries other than ‘.’ and ‘..’ was supplied to a remove directory or rename call.
.TP
\fBENOTSOCK()\fR
"Socket operation on non\-socket" Self\-explanatory.
.TP
\fBENOTSUP()\fR
"Not supported" The attempted operation is not supported for the type of object referenced.
.TP
\fBENOTTY()\fR
"Inappropriate ioctl for device" A control function (see `ioctl(2)`) was attempted for a file or special device for which the operation was inappropriate.
.TP
\fBENXIO()\fR
"No such device or address" Input or output on a special file referred to a device that did not exist, or made a request beyond the limits of the device. This error may also occur when, for example, a tape drive is not online or no disk pack is loaded on a drive.
.TP
\fBEOPNOTSUPP()\fR
"Operation not supported on socket" The attempted operation is not supported for the type of socket referenced; for example, trying to accept a connection on a datagram socket.
.TP
\fBEOVERFLOW()\fR
"Value too large to be stored in data type" A numerical result of the function was too large to be stored in the caller provided space.
.TP
\fBEPERM()\fR
"Operation not permitted" An attempt was made to perform an operation limited to processes with appropriate privileges or to the owner of a file or other resources.
.TP
\fBEPIPE()\fR
"Broken pipe" A write on a pipe, socket or FIFO for which there is no process to read the data.
.TP
\fBEPROTO()\fR
"Protocol error" Some protocol error occurred. This error is device\-specific, but is generally not related to a hardware failure.
.TP
\fBEPROTONOSUPPORT()\fR
"Protocol not supported" The protocol has not been configured into the system or no implementation for it exists.
.TP
\fBEPROTOTYPE()\fR
"Protocol wrong type for socket" A protocol was specified that does not support the semantics of the socket type requested. For example, you cannot use the ARPA Internet UDP protocol with type SOCK_STREAM.
.TP
\fBERANGE()\fR
"Numerical result out of range" A numerical result of the function was too large to fit in the available space (perhaps exceeded precision).
.TP
\fBEROFS()\fR
"Read\-only file system" An attempt was made to modify a file or directory was made on a file system that was read\-only at the time.
.TP
\fBESPIPE()\fR
"Illegal seek" An lseek function was issued on a socket, pipe or FIFO.
.TP
\fBESRCH()\fR
"No such process" No process could be found corresponding to that specified by the given process ID.
.TP
\fBESTALE()\fR
"Stale NFS file handle" An attempt was made to access an open file (on an NFS filesystem) which is now unavailable as referenced by the file descriptor. This may indicate the file was deleted on the NFS server or some other catastrophic event occurred.
.TP
\fBETIME()\fR
"STREAM ioctl() timeout" This error is reserved for future use.
.TP
\fBETIMEDOUT()\fR
"Operation timed out" A connect, connectx or send request failed because the connected party did not properly respond after a period of time. (The timeout period is dependent on the communication protocol.)
.TP
\fBETXTBSY()\fR
"Text file busy" The new process was a pure procedure (shared text) file which was open for writing by another process, or while the pure procedure file was being executed an open call requested write access.
.TP
\fBEWOULDBLOCK()\fR
"Operation would block" (may be same value as EAGAIN) (POSIX.1\-2001).
.TP
\fBEXDEV()\fR
"Improper link" A hard link to a file on another file system was attempted.
.TP
\fBsignal\fR
A container for all known "signal" constant values. Unsupported values have a default value of `0`.
.TP
\fBSIGHUP()\fR
Terminal line hangup.
.TP
\fBSIGINT()\fR
Interrupt program.
.TP
\fBSIGQUIT()\fR
Quit program.
.TP
\fBSIGILL()\fR
Illegal instruction.
.TP
\fBSIGTRAP()\fR
Trace trap.
.TP
\fBSIGABRT()\fR
Abort program.
.TP
\fBSIGIOT()\fR
An alias to `SIGABRT`
.TP
\fBSIGBUS()\fR
Bus error.
.TP
\fBSIGFPE()\fR
Floating\-point exception.
.TP
\fBSIGKILL()\fR
Kill program.
.TP
\fBSIGUSR1()\fR
User defined signal 1.
.TP
\fBSIGSEGV()\fR
Segmentation violation.
.TP
\fBSIGUSR2()\fR
User defined signal 2.
.TP
\fBSIGPIPE()\fR
Write on a pipe with no reader.
.TP
\fBSIGALRM()\fR
Real\-time timer expired.
.TP
\fBSIGTERM()\fR
Software termination signal.
.TP
\fBSIGCHLD()\fR
Child status has changed.
.TP
\fBSIGCONT()\fR
Continue after stop.
.TP
\fBSIGSTOP()\fR
Stop signal (cannot be caught or ignored).
.TP
\fBSIGTSTP()\fR
Stop signal generated from keyboard.
.TP
\fBSIGTTIN()\fR
Background read attempted from control terminal.
.TP
\fBSIGTTOU()\fR
Background write attempted to control terminal.
.TP
\fBSIGURG()\fR
Urgent condition present on socket.
.TP
\fBSIGXCPU()\fR
CPU time limit exceeded (see `setrlimit(2)`)
.TP
\fBSIGXFSZ()\fR
File size limit exceeded (see `setrlimit(2)`).
.TP
\fBSIGVTALRM()\fR
Virtual time alarm (see `setitimer(2)`).
.TP
\fBSIGPROF()\fR
Profiling timer alarm (see `setitimer(2)`).
.TP
\fBSIGWINCH()\fR
Window size change.
.TP
\fBSIGIO()\fR
I/O is possible on a descriptor (see `fcntl(2)`).
.TP
\fBSIGINFO()\fR
Status request from keyboard.
.TP
\fBSIGSYS()\fR
Non\-existent system call invoked.
